#: src/pages/docs/OverviewPage.tsx:43
msgid "Continuous output and fault isolation are design objectives, not warranties of uninterrupted operation. Inputs are sampled, never trusted to pace the output. A single fixed-cadence clock emits exactly one frame per tick. When a source drops, its tile holds its last good frame and shows a clear state while the engine reconnects in the background — the rest of the wall keeps running."
